From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:04:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: fail the run when no selected server answers (#153)

When all selected servers are down, or there is none to test, exit 1
and report each server's failure to stderr instead of emitting an
empty report. Runs with at least one successful server still exit 0.

The probe reads at most 512 bytes of the ping response instead of
all of it.

[Backported to 1.0.14, which has neither the NegotiatedTLS field nor
--json-stream: both are left out, the latter also from the tests.]

Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/librespeed/speedtest-cli/commit/8aefd77bd4bde428cd86d3622102f0ac0443d96e]
